title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf repo borrow
catalog: CLI command
target: mf repo borrow
summary: Borrow a repository of another machine, through a mount of its files

!! Reference

```
Borrow a repository of another machine, through a mount of its files

Its .metafolder is copied to --to, a new local directory, and the copy loaded: sync it with your repositories as with any other. The remote is marked borrowed meanwhile, and its own daemon refuses to load it; one that has it loaded refuses the borrow. `mf repo give-back` sends the copy home. Prints the repository's uuid.

Usage: mf repo borrow [OPTIONS] --to <TO> <ROOT>

Arguments:
  <ROOT>
          The remote repository's root, as mounted here (sshfs, NFS…)

Options:
      --to <TO>
          A new local directory to hold the copy's .metafolder

      --metafolder <METAFOLDER>
          The remote's .metafolder, when it is not inside its root

      --name <NAME>
          The copy's name here (default: the remote's), for a name already loaded

      --force
          Borrow past a holder file a crash of the remote daemon left

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
